course: dictionary
lesson: 10547
title: Unable and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Unable» means not able to do something, because you cannot or are not allowed to. It is built from «not» and «able», so you can see the meaning inside the word. You can be unable to come, unable to move, or unable to focus.
explain: Schools often use «unable» as a polite, formal way to say «can't». A letter might say, «If your child is unable to attend, please let us know.» It means the child cannot come, and the letter is being polite about it.
explain: Look for «to» after «unable». It is always followed by a verb, like «unable to reach» or «unable to swim». The opposite of unable is able: «She is able to swim» means she can swim.
fact: Unable means not able to do something, because you cannot or are not allowed to.
fact: «Unable» is always followed by «to» and a verb, as in «unable to come».
fact: The opposite of unable is able.
fact: «Breakfast can leave you wobbly and unable to focus.» Here unable means you cannot concentrate properly.
fact: Animals unable to fly, such as penguins and kiwis, cannot take off into the air.
exercise: «If your child is unable to attend, please let us know.» What does unable mean here? | Happy to come early | *Not able to come | Able to come at any time | Very eager to come
exercise: «Breakfast can leave you wobbly and unable to focus.» What does «unable to focus» mean? | *Cannot concentrate properly | Focusing very hard on a puzzle | Lost in a good book | Asleep at the desk
exercise: Which word is the opposite of unable? | Unfair | *Able | Table | Unhappy
test: Penguins are ___ to fly, so they swim and dive instead. | able | fast | *unable | happy
test: «Ella was unable to open the jar.» What does this tell you? | She bought a new jar | She opened it very quickly | She liked the jar very much | *She could not open it
exam: Which sentence uses «unable» correctly? | *He was unable to lift the box. | The box was unable heavy. | He lifted unable. | He was unable the box.
